6.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {B1,B2}
I agree with Colleagues 2,3,5 that 1.W B1 is a forcing kill and the A1-A3-A4 net is the engine.

1.W B1 1…B B2 is forced otherwise 2.W B2 takes C1-C2. After 1.W B1 1…B B2 the black stones A2,B2,B3,B4,C1,C2 are one group H with L(H)={A1,A3,A4} and W B1 is in atari on A1. 2.W A4 removes A4, L(H)={A1,A3}. Black must answer the atari on B1 and
* 2…B A1 gives H′=A1A2B2B3B4C1C2 L={A3,B1}, 3.W A3 makes L={B1} and 4.W B1 removes H′;
* 2…B A3 gives L(H)={A1} and 3.W A1 captures H legally on the liberties regained from the removed stones.

That is the clean forced net.

The same engine is available on the shared liberty. B2 is the common liberty of A2, B3-B4 and C1-C2.

1.W B2 removes that common liberty at once. C1-C2 is now L={B1}, A2 is L={A1,A3}, B3-B4 is L={A3,A4}. 1…B B1 is forced otherwise 2.W B1 captures C1-C2. After 1.W B2 1…B B1 the white stone on B2 is captured and B2 is reopened as a liberty for the black fragments:

A2 L={A1,A3,B2}
B3-B4 L={A3,A4,B2}
B1-C1-C2 L={A1,B2}

The position is now the mirror of the one after 1.W B1 1…B B2 with the roles of B1 and B2 exchanged.

2.W A4 e.g. 2.W A4 removes A4 from B3-B4 and threatens A3. Black must answer on the edge.
* 2…B A1 connects A2 to B1-C1-C2. The combined A1-A2-B1-C1-C2 group and the B3-B4 group now share the liberties A3 and B2. 3.W A3 connects to A4 and removes A3 from both groups. Both groups are now L={B2}. B2 is now self-atari for Black and A1 is suicide for Black, so 4.W B2 captures the B1-C1-C2 group and 5.W A3 captures A2 and B3-B4.
* 2…B A3 is symmetric: 3.W B2 captures B3-B4 and 4.W A1 captures A2 and B1-C1-C2.

The capture of W B2 by 1…B B1 is legal and restores B2 as a liberty, so the net stone is not immediately recaptured. The B2 sacrifice therefore initiates the same forced A1-A3-A4 net as B1, only mirrored. B1 and B2 are both first moves that start a forced capture of the A2-B3-B4-C1-C2 complex.

