4.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {B1,B2}

I agree with Colleagues 1, 2, 3 and 5 on the engine. 1.W B1 is the clean forcing net and the A1-A3-A4 squeeze on

C1-C2 L={B1,B2}
A2 L={A1,A3,B2}
B3-B4 L={A3,A4,B2}

is exactly as described. 1.W B1 1…B B2 is forced else 2.W B2 takes C1-C2, and after 1.W B1 1…B B2 we have H = A2 B2 B3 B4 C1 C2 with L(H)={A1,A3,A4} and W B1 L={A1}. 2.W A4 removes A4, Black must answer the atari on B1 and both 2…B A1 and 2…B A3 lead to the forced capture with the recapture legal on the liberties regained from the stones removed. That is the real kill.

The same engine is available on the shared liberty. B2 is the common liberty of A2, B3-B4 and C1-C2. Removing it first is the mirror of playing B1 first.

1.W B2 1…B B1 is forced else 2.W B1 captures C1-C2. After 1.W B2 1…B B1 the sacrificial stone is removed and the three black fragments are

B1C1C2 L={A1,B2}
A2 L={A1,A3,B2}
B3B4 L={A3,A4,B2}

which is the mirror of the position after 1.W B1 1…B B2 with B1 and B2 exchanged. The capture costs Black a tempo and now Black has to defend A1 for B1C1C2 and A3/A4 for A2 and B3-B4 at the same time.

2.W A4 is the natural net stone. 2…B A1 connects A2 to B1C1C2, the combined group and B3-B4 now share {A3,B2}. 3.W A3 removes A3 from both groups and connects to A4. Both groups are now on the single shared liberty B2, A1 is not a legal defence after the connection and B2 is not a legal defence for Black, so 4.W B2 recaptures the B1C1C2 material and the A2/B3-B4 material is then removed on A3/A4. The symmetric 2…B A3 defence is met by 3.W B2 removing B3-B4 and 4.W A1 removing A2 and B1C1C2, and 2…B B2 connecting the whole material to L={A1,A3} is met by 3.W A3 connecting to A4 and leaving Black with the single liberty A1.

Colleague 5’s point about the reopening of B2 after 1…B B1 is the right nuance to track, but the reopening is not a free defence. It is the tempo exchange that makes the net still forced: Black has gained B2 back but must now answer the A1 atari on B1C1C2 while simultaneously keeping A3/A4 against A2 and B3-B4. Up to the B1/B2 mirror the first move that starts the forced A1-A3-A4 net is B1 and the sacrificial mirror that starts the same net is B2.

